// Prop types. A prop's frame has its origin on the ground at the centre of its footprint and faces −Z.
// `colliders` are what paint and walking hit (boxes and cylinders, in metres), and stay the gameplay
// shape whatever draws the prop: a generated 3D `model` if it loads, else a `shape` the game builds in
// code from the colliders (game/world/PropShapes.cs: pallets, crate, tyres, drum, sandbags, barrier,
// desk, table_on_edge, filing_cabinet, racking, rubble, scrap, car_wreck, water_tower, cable_reel,
// generator, pump, skip, forklift, roller_door, container; for the rail yard, game/world/PropShapes.Railway.cs:
// box_van, open_wagon, flat_wagon, tank_wagon, shunter, buffer_stop, sleeper_stack, rail_stack; for the cold store,
// game/world/PropShapes.ColdStore.cs: lorry_trailer, pallet_racking, roll_cage, compressor, ammonia_tank, lorry_cab; for
// the hospital, game/world/PropShapes.Hospital.cs: hospital_bed, curtain_screen, locker_bank, medical_trolley,
// wheelchair, bench, operating_table, ambulance_wreck, fountain, boiler, chimney), else the colliders as greybox.
//   box:      center_m, size_m [x, y, z]
//   cylinder: center_m, radius_m, height_m (axis = +Y, tilt with rotation_deg)
//   rotation_deg [about X, about Y, about Z]; walk: false lets characters pass (paint still hits);
//   paint: false lets paint and sight through (it still blocks walking)
// Props at least 0.9 m tall count as cover for bots unless "cover": false.
